{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "He woke to the sound of birds chirping in perfect, looping cadence—too rhythmic, too clean—and the sunlight filtering through the trees had an unnatural golden hue, like a filter applied in post-production. His hand reached for his phone on the nightstand, but there was no nightstand. No phone. Just dew-damp grass beneath his bare feet and a faint, translucent HUD hovering at the corner of his vision: HP 100/100 | Quest: “Find the Old Man by the Bridge.” His own voice echoed in his head, not as memory but as a scripted line: “I’ve got to get moving.” He pinched his arm. It hurt. He screamed. The birds stopped. A chime sounded. “Player emotional response detected. Reward: +5 XP.” He looked down at his hands—slightly pixelated at the edges, like a low-res texture struggling to render.\n\n***\n\nHe ran through the forest, past NPCs who turned to face him with identical smiles, repeating the same three lines of dialogue every time he approached. A blacksmith offered “The Sword of Forgotten Names” for 100 gold—gold he didn’t have. A child asked him to “find her lost teddy bear,” and when he did, the bear vanished in a puff of sparkles, replaced by a quest completion animation. He found the Old Man by the bridge, who whispered, “You’re not supposed to be awake.” Then the sky fractured into polygons. The world glitched—a flicker of code, a floating menu labeled “Reset World?” with a blinking “YES” and “NO.” He didn’t know if he was the player… or the NPC. But as the Old Man faded into static, he whispered back, “Then what’s the win condition?” The screen blinked once. “You’re the boss fight now.”", "logprobs": [{"token": "He", "logprob": -0.3982396125793457}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -0.06083586812019348}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.03319094702601433}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -4.565611743601039e-05}, {"token": " sound", "logprob": -0.32585